#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Rebase and repair the upgrade docs of the current target version.

Reads the target from Chart.yaml "version:" and the baseline from
etc/release-baseline.yaml "upgrade_docs". Renames every
docs/_UPGRADE_PATHS/<old>-to-<target>-*.md to the baseline and fixes
titles, headings and cross-references. Creates missing docs as TODO stubs.

Also repairs the content against Chart.yaml and values.yaml:
  - upgrade doc: component version table and "## Changes" sections,
    adding missing rows and sorting them in values.yaml order
  - values-deltas doc: adds missing component sections and nested key
    added/removed lines
  - docs/images/images-<target>.yaml: fixes entries and adds missing ones;
    review the "name:"/"url:" of added entries by hand (ACR mirror name)
  - docs/images/images-baseline.yaml: regenerated
Issues it cannot fix are printed for manual review.

Run change-podiumd-baseline to change the baseline; this script never
writes release-baseline.yaml. Exits 1 when that file or key is missing.

Usage:
    fix-doc-consistency

Example:
    fix-doc-consistency
        # target 4.9.0, upgrade_docs "4.8.3": renames *-to-4.9.0-*.md
        # to 4.8.3-to-4.9.0-*.md and repairs their content
"""

